meta {
  name: 4d. Create POSTGIS DataSink (backs the OWS named API)
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/datasinks
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{sagaDataSetId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "dataSinkType": "POSTGIS",
    "configuration": {
      "tableName": "saga_workflow_observations",
      "dataStructureVersionId": "{{sagaDataStructureVersionId}}"
    }
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar('sagaPostgisDataSinkId', res.body.id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("DataSink created", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 201=created, 409=already exists from previous run
    expect(status === 201 || status === 409).to.be.true;
  });

  test("Has POSTGIS type", function() {
    if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
      expect(res.body.dataSinkType).to.equal('POSTGIS');
    }
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 4d of 18** — Prerequisites: dataset created (step 4) with its OWS named API, structure version released (step 3d).

  Creates the POSTGIS DataSink that backs the dataset's OWS named API. Release rejects an OWS named API with no POSTGIS sink behind it, because the route rewrites to a GeoServer workspace that is never provisioned — the published endpoint would 404. This sink is what makes the map surface complete and step 8 releasable.

  The sink is discovered by the saga via the dataset id, so it is deliberately not declared in the pipeline (step 5): the pipeline's flow ingests into FROST only, and adding a PostGIS branch would change what step 9d verifies.

  **Expected Response:** 201 Created, body contains `id` and `dataSinkType: "POSTGIS"`. 409 if the sink already existed (idempotent).

  **Post-condition:** Save `sagaPostgisDataSinkId` from `body.id` (deleted in cleanup step 12c).

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | DataSink record created in `portal_backend` DB, FK `dataset_id` → this dataset |
  | Config Adapter | — (table and GeoServer workspace are provisioned when the DATASET_CREATE saga runs in step 8) |
  | External System | — |
}
